    ["THERMAL FEA VERIFICATION", "Uniform insulated rod: L=1 m, A=1e-4 m2, k=10 W/(m K), q=10000 W/m3,", "T(0)=100 C, T(L)=20 C. Two-node elements use kA/h [1 -1; -1 1]", "and qAh/2 [1 1]. Both prescribed endpoints are correctly eliminated.", "Exact: T=100-80x/L+q*x*(L-x)/(2k).", "", "Elements    Nodes    Maximum midpoint error (C)    Ratio", "10          11       1.25                          -", "20          21       0.3125                        4.00", "40          41       0.078125                      4.00", "80          81       0.01953125                    4.00", "", "Errors use FE midpoint interpolation, not only nodes. Raw curves and", "convergence values are in results/thermal_N*.csv and thermal_convergence.csv.", "Debug insight: nodal error is near round-off whereas linear midpoint", "interpolation of the quadratic field has a nonzero error that converges 4x.", "", "PARALLEL PERFORMANCE", "Seed 20261102; 20,000 independent cases; 80 elements; warm-up plus five", "timed repetitions. Machine reported 16 logical CPUs; workers capped at 4.", "Medians: 1=54.581 ms; 2=28.682 ms, 1.903x, 95.1%; 3=20.047 ms,", "2.723x, 90.8%; 4=17.540 ms, 3.112x, 77.8%. Difference=0 C."],
